{"review":{"at":"2026-10-07T22:53:44-05:00","size":"full","verdict":"fix","findings":[{"n":1,"kind":"fix","text":"audit.mjs builds the ask id by slugging the title without lowercasing it (`ask.title?.replace(/[^a-z0-9]+/g,'-')`), so \"Memory: …\" becomes \"-emory-…\" and never matches the lowercase `id` that the ledger's later status lines use. Status updates are never merged into the ask, so every count in audit.json is wrong. Lowercase the title, or key on `ask.id`. Done that way, there are about 70 asks: 40 landed, 16 queued, 5 stalled, 3 parked, 3 dropped, 3 building."},{"n":2,"kind":"fix","text":"report.md's headline numbers don't match the script's own output. The report says \"259 total, 215 landed (83%)\"; audit.json says `total_asks: 105, landed: 0`. 258 is the ledger's line count, not its ask count. Rule 7 says numbers are computed, and this report's numbers weren't taken from the script."},{"n":3,"kind":"fix","text":"audit.mjs:159 computes `landed` as `unbuilt.filter(a => a.status === 'landed')`, which is always 0 because `unbuilt` only holds stalled/dropped/parked asks."},{"n":4,"kind":"fix","text":"Deliverable 1 isn't met for tasks. audit.mjs:44 `parseTasks()` walks every task.jsonl, but its result is never written to the output. About 51 task dirs from 09-30 to 10-07 have no `landed_at`, and none of them appear. There is also no \"stopped / never started / stale\" state anywhere, only landed vs building."},{"n":5,"kind":"fix","text":"Deliverable 2 asked for about 15 asks and got 5, and one of the 5 is \"Unnamed (empty title, 6 entries)\", which is an artifact of bug 1: those lines are status updates, not asks. Fixing the merge shows 16 queued asks that never started (e.g. \"Proposals: a Proposal class…\", \"Monitor: a Playwright agent on main…\", \"Now card: topics as nested sub-cards from refined prompts\") plus 5 stalled ones (\"Grip…\", \"Inbox: priority 50+…\", \"Framework home: grids without voids…\"). Those are exactly what the owner asked to see."},{"n":6,"kind":"fix","text":"Deliverable 3 says prompt refinement \"runs live on owner prompts via the Council system (`Server/council.mjs`)\", but council.mjs never mentions refine. The evidence that does exist is `ai2/faces.js` importing `prompt_modes` from `ext/Refine/prompt-card.js` and rendering `it.refined`. Say that, and note that the ask \"Prompts: each owner prompt becomes a refined Inbox card\" was dropped and the \"Now card … from refined prompts\" ask is still queued. The owner's question was whether this got built, and the honest answer is \"partly\"."},{"n":7,"kind":"fix","text":"Deliverable 4 claims \"No tasks were stopped due to usage wall or error\" without citing a source. The brief points to the Servex logs and log.jsonl, and nothing shows they were read. It also contradicts itself: \"5 entries … stalled\", then \"three later resumed\", then \"one remains stalled\", while the corrected ledger shows 5 still stalled. If the logs weren't searched, the answer should say \"unknown\"."},{"n":8,"kind":"fix","text":"The report's closing line \"The asks ledger is clean\" isn't supported. The ledger itself carries \"card corrected: … does not exist\" lines, and the report's own \"Unnamed\" entry shows the data was misread."},{"n":9,"kind":"fix","text":"The task never landed. task.jsonl has only the assign line, with no progress lines and no `landed_at`, so the board shows it as in flight. finish-task was required."},{"n":10,"kind":"note","text":"audit.mjs:7 hardcodes `C:\\\\Code\\\\lew42\\\\monorepo` as the repo root, so the script reads the main tree rather than the worktree it ran in (qf-6). Resolve the root from `import.meta.url` instead (four `..` up)."},{"n":11,"kind":"note","text":"A simpler approach: one reduce over asks.jsonl keyed on `id ?? slug(title)`, plus one pass over task.jsonl files, gives every number the report needs. It would fit in about 40 lines and would remove the hand-written figures."},{"n":12,"kind":"note","text":"report.md is longer than one screen, and its \"Script & Data\" section restates file names instead of linking them."}],"branch":"worktree/qf-6","head":"e102d04de9ebe0c4dd9afa8f08cda11213424ee3","model":"claude-opus-5-5","cost":0.5757482,"file":"review.md","report":null,"shots":null}}
